  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Bakit Mataas Ang Langit\n\nLong ago, the sky was very low, and there were
    no moon or stars. Have you ever wondered why the sky rose so high?\n\nMaria and
    her mother lived in a small nipa hut. Maria owned a golden comb and a necklace
    with shiny golden beads. \n\nEvery day, she would wear them and admire her reflection
    in the water, thinking, \u201CDo I look beautiful today?\u201D \n\nOne day, as
    Maria stared at her reflection, her mother called her.\n\n\u201CMaria, pound
    the rice!\u201D her mother said.\n\n\u201CYes, Mother,\u201D Maria replied, but
    she didn\u2019t move.\n\n\u201CHurry, Maria!\u201D her mother shouted. \u201CWe
    have no rice to cook!\u201D\n\n\u201CJust a moment!\u201D Maria answered, still
    staring at her reflection.\n\n\u201CMaria, I\u2019m telling you to pound some
    rice now. Hurry up,\u201D the mother ordered angrily.\n\nMaria stood up and went
    straight to the mortar and pestle. She knew that when her mother got very angry,
    she had to obey quickly.\n\nBecause of this, she didn\u2019t remove her comb
    and necklace and hurriedly started pounding rice. After a while, she began to
    sweat.\n\n\u201CMy necklace is getting soaked with sweat,\u201D she muttered.\n\nShe
    took off her jewelry and hung it on the low sky, which she could easily reach.
    \n\nAs she worked, she glanced at her comb and necklace. \u201CThey\u2019re so
    beautiful! I\u2019ll wear them again soon,\u201D she thought.\n\nTo finish faster,
    Maria lifted the pestle higher in order to slam it down harder. But each time
    she raised it, the pestle bumped the sky, pushing it upward. \n\nMaria didn\u2019t
    notice until the sky was too high to reach, making it impossible for her to recover
    the comb and necklace.\n\nEven though she was sad, she looked at the brighter
    side of things. That night, Maria looked up and saw her comb glowing as the moon
    and her beads twinkling as stars. \n\n\u201CMy comb shines even brighter now,\u201D
    she whispered, \u201Cand my necklace lights up the night!\u201D\n\n\u2013 THE
    END \u2013"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6619655a4e02543f482dc7e67a1dedf3, type: 2}
